= Autonomous agent — Simple =

An '''autonomous agent''' can make and carry out some decisions without a person telling it every next step.

For example, it may:

* choose an action;
* see what happened;
* change its plan;
* keep working toward a goal.

Autonomous does not mean “no rules.”

An agent can be autonomous inside strict limits, such as approved tools, budgets, safety rules, or required human approval for certain actions.

Autonomy also does not mean the system learns by itself.

